.TH TIME 1 "2026" "spicule" "spicule User Commands"
.SH NAME
time \- time a simple command
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B time
.RB [ \-p ]
.I utility
.RI [ argument .\|.\|.]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B time
runs
.I utility
(with any given
.I argument
operands) as a separate process, waits for it to finish, and then
writes a report of how long it took and how much processor time it
used to standard error \(em never to standard output, which is left
entirely to
.IR utility .
.PP
The elapsed ("real") time reported covers only
.IR utility 's
own run: it is measured immediately around starting and reaping
.IR utility ,
not
.BR time 's
own argument parsing or the search for
.I utility
along the command search path. The user and system time figures are
likewise specific to this one run of
.IR utility ,
isolated from any earlier command that may already have been run and
reaped in the same process (relevant, for example, when
.B time
is used repeatedly in one long-lived interactive session).
.PP
The report is always written in the form
.RS
.nf
real %f
user %f
sys %f
.fi
.RE
that is, three lines, each giving one figure as a decimal number of
seconds with at least one fractional digit (six is typical). This is
the exact format that is otherwise only guaranteed when
.B \-p
is given; this implementation always uses it, whether or not
.B \-p
was given on the command line.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-p
Accepted for compatibility with scripts that pass it; it has no effect
on the output format, since this implementation already always
produces the format described above.
.PP
A
.B \-\-
argument ends option parsing, so that a
.I utility
whose own name happens to begin with
.B \-
can still be named unambiguously.
.SH OPERANDS
.TP
.I utility
The command to run and time.
.TP
.I argument
Arguments to pass to
.IR utility .
.SH EXIT STATUS
If
.I utility
was found and ran, its own exit status is
.BR time 's
exit status, except that a
.I utility
terminated by a signal
.I n
is reported as
.RI ( 128 + n ).
Otherwise:
.TP
.B 1
No
.I utility
operand was given, an invalid option was given, or an internal failure
occurred while waiting for
.IR utility .
.TP
.B 126
.I utility
was found but could not be executed.
.TP
.B 127
.I utility
could not be found.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR timeout (1)
